    {
      "id": "7844bed6-08de-4ef6-902a-110fe33df586",
      "title": "Ready for the Day",
      "lyrics": "[Instrumental Intro: groovy electric bass, bright brass stabs, shaker]\n\n[Verse 1]\nThe alarm went off, I let it ring\nThen got up before the second ding\nThere's a shirt I like behind the chair\nA little wrinkled, I don't care\nYesterday I lost my nerve\nHad a few things not quite work\nBut the kettle's on, my shoes are tied\nI'm taking one more step outside\n\n[Pre-Chorus]\nI don't need to have it figured out\nTo get my feet back on the ground\nTake a breath and turn the key\nThere's a whole day waiting for me\n\n[Chorus]\nI'm ready for the day\nLet a little sunshine hit my face\nI've got a heart that won't give up\nAnd a friend who says, you've got this, love\nI'm ready for the day\nEven if a few things go astray\nOne good step, then another one\nHere I come, here I come\n\n[Verse 2]\nAt the corner someone's singing\nOff-key, but I like the feeling\nBuy a coffee, call my friend\nShe says, tell me how it went\nI say, ask me when it's over\nRight now I'm a little bolder\nI've been waiting for a perfect sign\nMaybe showing up will do just fine\n\n[Pre-Chorus]\nI don't need to have it figured out\nTo get my feet back on the ground\nTake a breath and turn the key\nThere's a whole day waiting for me\n\n[Chorus]\nI'm ready for the day\nLet a little sunshine hit my face\nI've got a heart that won't give up\nAnd a friend who says, you've got this, love\nI'm ready for the day\nEven if a few things go astray\nOne good step, then another one\nHere I come, here I come\n\n[Instrumental Drop: joyful brass motif over melodic house groove]\n\n[Bridge: intimate, breathing room]\nSome mornings I still hesitate\nStand by the door and make you wait\nYou squeeze my hand, I laugh a little\nI can start right in the middle\nNot every try will turn to gold\nBut there's a story left untold\nAnd I want to see where this one goes\n\n[Final Chorus: joyful, expressive]\nI'm ready for the day\nLet a little sunshine hit my face\nI've got a heart that won't give up\nAnd a friend who says, you've got this, love\nI'm ready for the day\nEven if a few things go astray\nOne good step, then another one\nHere I come, here I come\n\n[Outro]\nOne good step, then another one\nI'm ready for the day\n[Brass and bass outro]",
      "style": "English dance-pop / melodic house, 122 BPM, bright major key, energetic optimistic mood. Warm intimate slightly husky female mezzo-soprano, airy verses, rounded midrange, smooth head voice; preserve previous vocal direction. Human expressive singing: audible gentle breaths, meaning-led pauses, varied word stress and dynamics, subtle behind-the-beat phrasing, light end-phrase vibrato, occasional natural rasp, conversational verses growing into joyful chorus. No robotic timing, hard tuning, excessive melisma or shrill belting. New 8-second instrumental intro: groovy fingerstyle electric bass riff, answered by bright brass stabs, shaker joining gradually. No piano, guitar or marimba-led opening. Four-on-the-floor kick, warm bass, shimmering synths, uplifting singalong hook within 25 seconds, melodic drop reprising brass motif. Around 3 minutes, upfront clear vocal, spacious stereo, balanced bass, natural production.",
      "type": "vocal",
      "vocalGender": "female",
      "personaRef": null,
      "model": "kie-suno-v5.5",
