    {
      "id": "b7956cb0-29af-42a5-9228-fc5e9514f23c",
      "title": "Crown of Ashes",
      "lyrics": "[Intro: low cello pulse, distant French horn, unfolding strings]\n\n[Verse 1: intimate low baritone]\nI found my father's coat downstairs\nStill hanging where he left it\nI put it on to face the cold\nAnd stood there for a second\nThe house was quiet as a church\nThe clock kept counting through it\nI had a thousand things to say\nAnd no one left to say them to\n\n[Pre-Chorus: tension rising]\nI cannot bring the old days back\nOr make these walls forget\nBut I can turn the handle\nWith the strength that I have left\n\n[Chorus: towering orchestra, expressive falsetto hook]\nI won't wear a crown of ashes\nI won't make a throne of pain\nLet the wind take what it carries\nI am stepping out again\nI can grieve and still keep going\nI can fall and still stand tall\nI won't wear a crown of ashes\nThere's a life beyond these walls\n\n[Verse 2: restrained dark-pop pulse]\nThe street was busy, bright and strange\nA child ran past me laughing\nI almost turned around for home\nThen heard my brother asking\nAre you coming by tonight?\nWe saved a place beside us\nI said I'd try, then crossed the road\nBefore the fear could find me\n\n[Pre-Chorus: brass and percussion build]\nI cannot bring the old days back\nBut I can keep their kindness\nA place for someone at my table\nA lamp left on in darkness\n\n[Chorus: full strings, brass, taiko]\nI won't wear a crown of ashes\nI won't make a throne of pain\nLet the wind take what it carries\nI am stepping out again\nI can grieve and still keep going\nI can fall and still stand tall\nI won't wear a crown of ashes\nThere's a life beyond these walls\n\n[Instrumental: sweeping string ostinato, French horns, taiko and timpani]\n\n[Bridge: stripped back, breath and natural rasp]\nSome nights I still reach for the phone\nTo tell you something small\nAnd when I hear your words in mine\nI haven't lost it all\nYou taught me how to mend a chair\nAnd how to ask for help\nToday I let my brother in\nInstead of blaming myself\n\n[Final Chorus: immense, soaring falsetto on title]\nI won't wear a crown of ashes\nI won't make a throne of pain\nLet the wind take what it carries\nI am stepping out again\nI can grieve and still keep going\nI can fall and still stand tall\nI won't wear a crown of ashes\nThere's a life beyond these walls\n\n[Outro: powerful orchestra, warm low vocal]\nI'll leave a lamp on in the hall\nThere's a life beyond these walls\n[Extended orchestral resolution: brass, timpani, lingering low strings]",
      "style": "Epic orchestral cinematic, sweeping string ostinato and broad legato violins, bold French horns and low brass, deep orchestral percussion with driving taiko and timpani, retain a dark-pop pulse through restrained synth bass and modern kick, intimate low male lead rising into expressive falsetto on the hooks, dramatic builds from sparse verse to towering chorus, wide polished film-score mix with clear vocal center and powerful final outro. Original English song, dark minor key, 88 BPM, around 3:30. Distinctive warm gritty baritone, textured husky rasp, resonant chest voice, natural breath and slight vocal cracks, emotionally varied phrasing, light vibrato. Falsetto retains an airy human texture; no screaming, robotic tuning or harsh distortion. Intro: low cello pulse and distant horn, then strings unfold. Defiant renewal after personal loss. Quiet bridge before immense final chorus, orchestral outro resolving with lingering low strings.",
      "type": "vocal",
      "vocalGender": "male",
      "personaRef": null,
      "model": "kie-suno-v5.5",
      "modelLabel": "KIE AI Suno V5.5",
      "credits": 11,
      "status": "success",
